  "protocol": {
    "preprocessing": "Existing native256 frozen ConvNeXt mean768+population spatial std768. Per-bank mean/population variance on outertrain320 only; scale_j=max(std_j, train-bank RMSstd), allzero bank unit scales. Common centered1536-feature matrix. No PCA whitening and no post-PCA scaling; both arms use same feature metric.",
    "PCA": "Centered outertrain float64 full SVD, keep first128 right singular vectors only in control. Full Ridge retains all feature directions; SVD is a solver, not dimensionality truncation in full arm.",
    "ridge": "Minimize ||y_standardized-Z beta||^2 + alpha||beta||^2. Training target mean/std, unpenalized intercept. Alpha separately solves sum(lambda_i/(lambda_i+alpha))=32 from train-X Gram eigenvalues lambda_i=s_i^2. Fixed df32 excludes intercept; total conditional linear smoother df33. No y-dependent alpha choice, no alpha grid, no inner model selection.",
    "advancement_gate": "Full Ridge must beat PCA128 Ridge overall standalone and fixed10% blend, with >=3/5 positive paired blend folds. Also fixed10% blend must improve021>=.02 with>=3/5 folds, conditional groupbootstrap CI95 lower>0, improvement after removing largest5 benefit rows>0. No dimension/df/blend rescue if failed. Even if passed, report to parent before resplits or other expansion."
  },
  "limits": [
    "Both arms are Ridge readouts; results do not identify the effect of removing PCA from the nonlinear191 MLP.",
    "Full Ridge preserves nonzero directions but shrinks leading and remaining components differently at the same effective df; this is a matched-complexity soft-versus-hard truncation pipeline comparison.",
    "Equal effective degrees of freedom does not guarantee equal estimator variance or equal bias.",
    "No post-PCA scaling/whitening in either arm, unlike191 post-PCA MLP scaling; pre-PCA bank scalers and PCA128 subspace match191.",
    "Reused development400; conditional bootstrap not independent validation or corrected for historical model selection."
